{"kind": "local_or_unclassified_prose", "line": 87, "review_required": true, "scope_stack": [], "text_excerpt": "A good example to keep in mind is the following. Suppose that $S = \\bigcup S_i$ is an open covering. In that case we have seen descent data for sheaves of sets in Sheaves, Section \\ref{sheaves-section-glueing-sheaves} where we called them ``glueing data for sheaves of sets with respect to the given covering''. Moreover, we proved that the category of glueing data is equivalent to the category of sheaves on $S$. We will show the analogue in the setting above when $\\{S_i \\to S\\}_{i\\in I}$ is an fpqc covering."}
